# Test: a directive NAME must be an IDENTIFIER — `directive 42` is refused.
#
# The NAME half of the same grammar rule `directive_value_int_error.gg` pins on
# the VALUE half:
#
#     directive = "directive" IDENTIFIER { "-" IDENTIFIER } [ "=" IDENTIFIER ]
#
# Rust gg refuses it at parse time (`expected identifier, found integer 42`).
# Before this round the self-host ACCEPTED it and emitted `int main(` — measured
# — because `token_ident` returns "" for an integer token and the empty name then
# flowed into an AST nobody validated.
#
# ⚠ This cell is NOT in the divergence matrix `todo/t0825` was filed with; it was
# found by re-running that matrix's grammar axis with the name slot varied
# instead of the value slot. It and `directive_trailing_token_error.gg` are the
# 14th and 15th divergent cells.
#
# Pinned on BOTH lanes: `directive_name_not_identifier_error` (Rust gg) and
# `sh_rejects_directive_name_not_identifier` (self-host driver).

directive 42

void main():
    print("REACHED — the directive name was NOT validated on this lane")
